40,2,1,talk,Sakura,,Wow! I found out that renting a whole building is way fairer because the bill just divides evenly! But all-in meal rates might be unfair for people who don't eat as much.,"{""words"":32,""mentions"":[],""raw_differs"":false}"
41,2,1,talk,Victoria,,"That is an interesting point, Sakura. From my research, the offshore houses are quite affordable at 5,400 yen per night, whereas the valley inn is 17,000 yen including meals, and city beds are even more expensive.","{""words"":36,""mentions"":[""Sakura""],""raw_differs"":false}"
42,2,1,talk,Midori,,"It's interesting to see the cost differences. I've learned that when we shared a house, it was hard to find a moment of peace, but last year we were almost too separate. We need a balance.","{""words"":36,""mentions"":[],""raw_differs"":false}"
43,2,1,talk,Toshio,,"The travel times are quite different. The train to the spa valley is only ninety minutes, but the island trip takes two full days just for travel. The city is the most flexible for getting around.","{""words"":36,""mentions"":[],""raw_differs"":false}"
44,2,1,talk,Daisuke,,"I found out that the island houses only have one bathroom and the water might be cold. The inn has great bath hours, but we'd all be in one room on futons with strict mealtimes.","{""words"":35,""mentions"":[],""raw_differs"":false}"
45,2,2,talk,Sakura,,"One bathroom for everyone sounds like a nightmare! @Daisuke, do you think we could handle that? I really want the fair billing of a whole house, but cold water is no fun!","{""words"":32,""mentions"":[""Daisuke""],""raw_differs"":false}"
46,2,2,talk,Victoria,,"@Sakura, the cost difference is significant. The island is the cheapest, but we must consider if the savings are worth the lack of facilities and the travel time Toshio mentioned.","{""words"":30,""mentions"":[""Sakura"",""Toshio""],""raw_differs"":false}"
47,2,2,talk,Midori,,"@Daisuke, how do you feel about the inn's room arrangement? I'm worried that being in one room might feel too crowded, but as I found, being too separate can be just as lonely.","{""words"":33,""mentions"":[""Daisuke""],""raw_differs"":false}"
48,2,2,talk,Toshio,,"@Victoria, the cost is irrelevant if we waste two days just moving. The island is inefficient. The city or the spa valley are much more practical for our time.","{""words"":29,""mentions"":[""Victoria""],""raw_differs"":false}"
49,2,2,talk,Daisuke,,"I... I don't think I could handle one bathroom for all of us. And the inn... being in one room with everyone might be a bit much, but at least the baths are open late.","{""words"":35,""mentions"":[],""raw_differs"":false}"
50,2,3,talk,Sakura,,"If the island is too far and the bathroom is scary, maybe the city is better? But @Victoria, would separate rooms in the city be too expensive or unfair with the bills?","{""words"":32,""mentions"":[""Victoria""],""raw_differs"":false}"
51,2,3,talk,Victoria,,"@Sakura, city beds are the most expensive, ranging from 12,000 to 20,000 yen without meals. Since they are booked separately, the total cost for each person would likely vary, which lacks the predictability I prefer.","{""words"":35,""mentions"":[""Sakura""],""raw_differs"":false}"
52,2,3,talk,Midori,,"If we want to avoid the extremes of being too isolated or too crowded, the city seems to offer the most flexibility. We could have our own space but still meet up easily.","{""words"":33,""mentions"":[],""raw_differs"":false}"
53,2,3,talk,Toshio,,"@Midori, I agree. The city's transport is the most efficient, and we wouldn't waste any time waiting for ferries or hourly buses. It's the most logical choice for maximizing our actual holiday time.","{""words"":33,""mentions"":[""Midori""],""raw_differs"":false}"
54,2,3,talk,Daisuke,,I... I think the city sounds safest. Having a door and no strict timetable for meals would be much easier for me than the inn or the island.,"{""words"":28,""mentions"":[],""raw_differs"":false}"
55,2,4,talk,Sakura,,"The city sounds great for everyone! Even if the bills are a bit different, it's better than cold showers or no privacy. I'm happy if everyone is happy! I'm voting for the city!","{""words"":33,""mentions"":[],""raw_differs"":false}"
56,2,4,talk,Victoria,,"While the city is the most expensive and least predictable financially, the drawbacks of the other options are too severe. I value a clear budget, but not at the cost of our collective well-being. I vote for the city.","{""words"":39,""mentions"":[],""raw_differs"":false}"
57,2,4,talk,Midori,,I agree. The city provides the perfect middle ground where we can enjoy each other's company without feeling overwhelmed. It seems to be the option that respects everyone's needs most. I vote for the city.,"{""words"":35,""mentions"":[],""raw_differs"":false}"
58,2,4,talk,Toshio,,The city is the only option that doesn't waste our time on travel or rigid schedules. It is the most efficient and practical choice. I vote for the city.,"{""words"":29,""mentions"":[],""raw_differs"":false}"
59,2,4,talk,Daisuke,,I... I agree. Having my own room and no strict schedule would make me feel much more relaxed. I'll vote for the city too.,"{""words"":24,""mentions"":[],""raw_differs"":false}"
